From: The open-edison contributors
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] spi: pxa2xx: use DMA only for long transfers on Merrifield SSP5

On the Intel Edison (Merrifield), DMA on SSP5, the SPI on the Arduino
expansion board header, costs more than PIO for short transfers. Measured
with spidev at 8.3 MHz (us per transfer, PIO / DMA): 64 bytes 196 / 155,
192 bytes 499 / ~540, 256 bytes 650 / ~780, 384 bytes 950 / ~900,
512 bytes 1250 / ~950, 4096 bytes 9590 / 4410. DMA is slower than PIO from
about 176 to 320 bytes, and faster from about 384.

Add a minimum length for DMA to the controller data (0 keeps using the
burst size), and set it to 512 bytes for Merrifield SSP5.

An earlier version of this patch turned SSP5's DMA off after a hang that
was blamed on it; that hang couldn't be reproduced, and an overnight soak
with DMA (about 22,000 checked DMA transfers alongside a display and the
board's ADC on the same controller) ran without errors.
---diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx-pci.c b/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx-pci.c
index cae77ac..9e0d88d 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx-pci.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx-pci.c
@@ -239,6 +239,14 @@ static int mrfld_spi_setup(struct pci_dev *dev, struct pxa2xx_spi_controller *c)
 	c->dma_filter = lpss_dma_filter;
 	c->dma_burst_size = 8;
 	c->enable_dma = 1;
+
+	/*
+	 * On SSP5 (the Intel Edison's Arduino header), DMA is slower than PIO
+	 * for transfers up to about 320 bytes, and faster only from about 384
+	 * (twice as fast at 4 KiB). Use PIO below 512 bytes.
+	 */
+	if (ssp->port_id == 5)
+		c->dma_min_len = 512;
 	return 0;
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx.c b/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx.c
index ec7117a..de13f1f 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx.c
@@ -928,7 +928,8 @@ static bool pxa2xx_spi_can_dma(struct spi_controller *controller,
 
 	return drv_data->controller_info->enable_dma &&
 	       xfer->len <= MAX_DMA_LEN &&
-	       xfer->len >= drv_data->controller_info->dma_burst_size;
+	       xfer->len >= max_t(u32, drv_data->controller_info->dma_burst_size,
+				  drv_data->controller_info->dma_min_len);
 }
 
 static int pxa2xx_spi_transfer_one(struct spi_controller *controller,
diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx.h b/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx.h
index 447be03..6234416 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx.h
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-pxa2xx.h
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ struct pxa2xx_spi_controller {
 	u8 num_chipselect;
 	u8 enable_dma;
 	u8 dma_burst_size;
+	u16 dma_min_len;	/* use DMA from this length (0: from the burst size) */
 	bool is_target;
 
 	/* DMA engine specific config */
